# Scout ignore patterns. Same shape as .gitignore.
#
# How lines are interpreted:
#   - Bare directory names (no slash, no wildcard, no leading "!")
#     feed the fast directory-prune optimisation in os.walk — these
#     subtrees are never descended into. Use them for caches, build
#     output, vendored dependencies.
#   - Anything else (contains "/", "*", "?", or starts with "!") falls
#     through to per-file fnmatch and is matched against the path
#     relative to the repo root, plus the bare filename.
#
# scout install drops this template into <repo>/.scoutignore on first
# `scout index` if no .scoutignore exists. Edit per-repo to add project-
# specific exclusions (e.g. `**/Third Party/**`, `vendor/`, `*.generated.cs`).

# VCS
.git
.svn
.hg

# Editors / IDEs
.vs
.idea
.vscode

# Python
__pycache__
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.venv
venv
env

# JS / Node
node_modules
.next
.nuxt

# Lockfiles + machine-generated content — no useful code, but
# vendored/minified files routinely chunk to 800-1500 embeddings each,
# exhausting the CUDA arena and collapsing throughput.
# Leading `*` makes these globs (classifier needs `*`/`?`/`/`/`!`);
# fnmatch's `*` matches any chars including `/`, so one pattern catches
# both root-level and nested occurrences.
*.lock
*package-lock.json
*pnpm-lock.yaml
*go.sum
*.min.js
*.min.css

# Build output
dist
build
out
bin
obj

# .NET / NuGet
packages
TestResults

# C/C++ / JVM dependency caches
vcpkg_installed
.gradle

# Web / generated
wwwroot
coverage
cldr-data

# Scout itself
.scout
# --- scout managed defaults: edit above or below, not inside ---
# Scout ignore patterns. Similar to .gitignore, but NOT identical — read the
# two rules below before adding a line, because a wrong pattern matches nothing
# and says nothing.
#
# How lines are interpreted:
#   - Bare directory names (no slash, no wildcard, no leading "!")
#     feed the fast directory-prune optimisation in os.walk — these
#     subtrees are never descended into. Use them for caches, build
#     output, vendored dependencies. ALWAYS the first choice.
#   - Anything else (contains "/", "*", "?", or starts with "!") falls
#     through to per-file fnmatch and is matched against the path
#     relative to the repo root, plus the bare filename.
#
# THREE FORMS THAT SILENTLY MATCH NOTHING — all three look right:
#   package-lock.json   a bare FILE name goes to the directory-prune set,
#                       and matches no directory.      Use *package-lock.json
#   perf/history/       a trailing slash is a .gitignore habit; this is
#                       tested against `perf/history/run.json`, and a
#                       pattern ending in "/" never matches a file.
#   */perf/history/*    paths are matched RELATIVE TO THE REPO ROOT, so a
#                       root-level `perf/` has no leading component for the
#                       `*/` to consume. Works nested, fails at the root.
#
# To exclude a directory that is not a bare name, glue the leading star:
#   *perf/history/*     matches at the root AND at any depth.
#
# Verify with `scout-index prune-ignored . --dry-run` and READ THE COUNT.
# Zero matches on a directory you know is indexed means the pattern is wrong.
#
# scout install drops this template into <repo>/.scoutignore on first
# `scout index` if no .scoutignore exists. Edit per-repo to add project-
# specific exclusions (e.g. `*Third Party/*`, `*vendor/*`, `*.generated.cs`).
#
#   - Large vendored artefacts are read and discarded on every run. Files
#     over 2 MB are skipped by symbol extraction and over ~2 MB by the embed
#     cap, but they are still READ first. If your repo carries vendored API-doc
#     XML beside a third-party DLL, a WiX-generated script, or similar, add
#     the pattern here — e.g. `**/Third Party/**` or `*.xml` scoped to that
#     directory. Check `.scout/extraction-warnings.log` after a run: every
#     oversize skip is named there.

# Claude Code worktrees — `.claude/worktrees/` duplicates every tracked
# file. Without this prune, GDScript (and every language) indexes each
# script N times and pollutes the `res://` project-root resolver.
# `.claude-worktrees/` is a SIBLING, not a child: bare names prune by exact
# directory name, so `.claude` does not cover it. Listed separately rather
# than globbed as `.claude*` so both keep the zero-cost directory prune —
# a glob would fall through to per-file fnmatch on every file in the repo.
.claude
.claude-worktrees

# Godot build cache — `.godot/imported/` holds generated `.res` import
# artefacts, not source. A single imported `.glb` chunks past the embed
# cap (1,252 chunks observed on a real project), so it gets scanned,
# chunked, then skipped — burning scan time and leaving a dead row.
.godot

# Line-delimited JSON — an append-only log format, not source. One
# orchestrator log produced 29,291 chunks against a 1,000 cap, so every
# index read the whole file, chunked it, then threw the work away and
# left the Embedding bar a unit short of its total. `.ndjson` is the same
# format under its other common extension.
*.jsonl
*.ndjson

# Vendored example code — a vendored library's `examples/` tree dominates
# messaging graphs. Anchored under a vendoring root (leading `*` spans `/`)
# so first-party `examples/` and `src/examples/` stay indexed; a bare
# `**/examples/**` would over-exclude them.
*vendor/**/examples/**
*third_party/**/examples/**

# MSVC / VC++ build output — `Debug`/`Release` are the standard configuration
# directories and `*.res`/`*.recipe` are compiler intermediates. A local build
# churns these, so without the prune every incremental run re-embeds build
# output (a 1,160-chunk `.res` binary was observed tripping the oversize skip).
# NOT `Win32`: it is also a common .NET convention for P/Invoke wrapper source
# directories, and a bare name here feeds the os.walk prune — the exclusion
# would be total and silent. Same reasoning keeps `x64` out.
Debug
Release
*.res
*.recipe

# MSVC project files — file listings and GUIDs, not source. Measured on a
# 35,650-file C++ corpus: 207 .vcxproj + 162 .vcxproj.filters carrying 6,887
# chunks, 3.2% of the whole index, and one .vcxproj chunks to 1,667 against
# the 1,000-chunk cap — read, chunked and discarded on every run. Same
# argument that seeded *.res and *.recipe.
*.vcxproj
*.vcxproj.filters

# Static-site / doc-generator output dirs. docfx `_site/` and Sphinx
# `_build/` are generated trees: one client `_site/` directory accounted
# for every unindexable file, the three slowest extractions, and both
# annotation poison files in a report. Bare names so the os.walk prune
# never descends into them (the fast path). A user who wants one indexed
# can negate it (e.g. `!_site`) OUTSIDE this block — the line survives
# every refresh. Existing rows from a prior index need `scout prune-ignored`.
_site
_build
# --- end scout managed defaults ---
